# NEX ERP — Cursor & AI Rules

You are working on NEX ERP. Every modification MUST strictly comply with these clean code rules:

1. Coupling & Cohesion:
   - Frontend: Tri-Layer Colocation per route folder (`_components/`, `_hooks/`, `_types/`, entry `page.tsx`).
   - Backend: Domain Sub-Services orchestrated by thin Facade Orchestrators (< 250 lines).
2. File Size Limits:
   - `page.tsx` < 120 lines (max limit 150).
   - Backend Facades < 250 lines.
   - Sub-services / Components < 300–400 lines.
3. Cognitive Complexity: Single responsibility, low cognitive complexity.
4. Zero Dead Code: Check `docs/ROUTE_MAP.md`. Never create duplicate/fossil routes.
5. UI Integrity: 0% visual regression. Use `@/components/dna`.
6. Strict Type Safety: Strict TypeScript. Verify with `npm run typecheck` (both frontend and backend) and `npm --prefix frontend run build`.
